/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 50 0 R
/T (In this experiment, a custom function named generateApplicationID was created with the Deluge language, the Default namespace, the string return type and two string arguments in the Student Admission application. The function was saved, listed in the Functions section and executed successfully, returning the expected confirmation message for the supplied applicant name. Although the function was simple, it illustrates the procedure for creating, executing and verifying a custom function. Combining low-code development with suitable pro-code extensions can support more flexible application development, in which standard functionality is built visually and specific logic is added through code where it is required.)
/E (In this experiment, a custom function named generateApplicationID was created with the Deluge language, the Default namespace, the string return type and two string arguments in the Student Admission application. The function was saved, listed in the Functions section and executed successfully, returning the expected confirmation message for the supplied applicant name. Although the function was simple, it illustrates the procedure for creating, executing and verifying a custom function. Combining low-code development with suitable pro-code extensions can support more flexible application development, in which standard functionality is built visually and specific logic is added through code where it is required.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
